1
00:00:05,467 --> 00:00:12,533
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,733
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:43,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,367 --> 00:00:46,567
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,833 --> 00:00:57,000
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,967 --> 00:00:59,800
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,933 --> 00:01:00,933
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:01,033 --> 00:01:02,633
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,767 --> 00:01:04,433
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,467
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:11,667
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:17,167
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:19,500
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,033
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:24,867
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,533 --> 00:01:28,500
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:31,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:33,533 --> 00:01:35,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:35,367 --> 00:01:36,333
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,467 --> 00:01:37,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,867 --> 00:01:39,100
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:42,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:49,667
<i>One hundred pesos
to become part of Anino.</i>

24
00:01:50,533 --> 00:01:51,567
<i> I'll think about it.</i>

25
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:53,667
<i> What I don't understand, Pops,</i>

26
00:01:53,767 --> 00:01:56,533
<i>is why you're so impressed
with him.</i>

27
00:01:56,667 --> 00:01:59,500
<i>Out of all our members,
he's the weakest.</i>

28
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,733
<i>- Who left this?
- No one, Gabo.</i>

29
00:02:03,733 --> 00:02:05,667
<i> Victor Zafra alias "Tiger."</i>

30
00:02:05,767 --> 00:02:08,333
<i>Mr. Chan will have
a transaction,</i>

31
00:02:08,433 --> 00:02:10,400
<i>and it's likely
with Victor Zafra.</i>

32
00:02:10,567 --> 00:02:11,567
<i> This is our mission.</i>

33
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:13,800
<i>We have to keep Mr. Chan
under surveillance</i>

34
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:16,933
<i>from his jewelry store
until he leaves.</i>

35
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:18,333
<i> We will follow him anywhere</i>

36
00:02:18,467 --> 00:02:21,100
<i>because he's our lead to where
the transaction will take place.</i>

37
00:02:21,233 --> 00:02:24,433
If you're watching this video...

38
00:02:25,567 --> 00:02:29,033
<i>...it means you've accepted
the mission.</i>

39
00:02:29,133 --> 00:02:35,400
<i>Tiger leads the largest gold
smuggling operations</i>

40
00:02:35,533 --> 00:02:36,600
<i> in the country.</i>

41
00:02:36,733 --> 00:02:40,933
<i>Your mission, Gabo, is
to bring us Victor Zafra</i>

42
00:02:41,067 --> 00:02:43,433
<i> dead or alive.</i>

43
00:02:45,633 --> 00:02:46,933
[DOORS OPENING, CREAKING]

44
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:52,800
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

45
00:02:52,967 --> 00:02:53,800
Lucas.

46
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,133
Tomorrow...

47
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:01,467
Come with me
when I meet with Mr. Chan.

48
00:03:04,067 --> 00:03:05,367
Papa is right.

49
00:03:06,433 --> 00:03:08,100
You have to learn the business
at an early age.

50
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:10,100
[LUCAS INHALES DEEPLY]

51
00:03:10,933 --> 00:03:11,800
Wait.

52
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,467
How--

53
00:03:13,633 --> 00:03:16,467
- How are you? Are you okay?
- I'm fine, Victor.

54
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:20,967
I can actually fight against
Stallone and Harris.

55
00:03:22,133 --> 00:03:23,633
I just let them beat me.

56
00:03:24,467 --> 00:03:25,833
I know you can win against them.

57
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:29,500
I know you can,
but I'm your older brother.

58
00:03:29,633 --> 00:03:32,833
You can't stop me from
protecting you against anyone.

59
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:35,900
Thank you, brother.

60
00:03:38,533 --> 00:03:39,833
But I am no longer a child.

61
00:03:40,967 --> 00:03:42,100
I can handle myself.

62
00:03:43,667 --> 00:03:45,133
And I'll prove that to you.

63
00:03:46,333 --> 00:03:48,000
[PATTING]

64
00:03:48,133 --> 00:03:55,000
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

65
00:04:04,867 --> 00:04:05,700
[KAREN] Oh.

66
00:04:07,067 --> 00:04:08,000
Sam!

67
00:04:08,133 --> 00:04:11,500
It's good you were able
to handle Ma'am Pia.

68
00:04:11,633 --> 00:04:12,933
It wasn't obvious
that you were nervous.

69
00:04:13,567 --> 00:04:15,133
- Really?
- Mm-hmm!

70
00:04:15,233 --> 00:04:19,333
Gosh, I was so nervous.
My heart was pounding so fast.

71
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:21,033
I just gathered the courage
to speak.

72
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:24,433
But I also just told myself
this isn't for Ma'am Pia.

73
00:04:24,567 --> 00:04:26,200
This is for our country.

74
00:04:26,367 --> 00:04:28,767
I know that,
that's why you're my idol.

75
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:31,833
But, you know,
I was actually shaking earlier.

76
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:34,200
- You were shaking in fear?
- No.

77
00:04:34,367 --> 00:04:36,000
I was shaking in frustration,
in anger!

78
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:37,533
Ma'am Pia's so frustrating!

79
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:39,333
She keeps looking
for gaps and shortcomings,

80
00:04:39,433 --> 00:04:41,033
and she'll turn it
into a huge issue!

81
00:04:41,167 --> 00:04:42,700
She's so annoying.
I wanted to squeeze her!

82
00:04:42,833 --> 00:04:43,867
Calm down.

83
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:47,467
You know we're not doing this
to ask for praise, right?

84
00:04:47,567 --> 00:04:49,867
Or to get recognition
in the NCIA.

85
00:04:50,033 --> 00:04:51,033
We're doing this

86
00:04:51,167 --> 00:04:54,300
to lessen the number
of criminals in this country.

87
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:56,200
[SAM BREATHES DEEPLY]

88
00:04:56,367 --> 00:04:58,633
That includes that annoying man.

89
00:05:00,767 --> 00:05:07,733
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

90
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,033
Yeah, sure.

91
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:29,700
Yeah, okay.

92
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,733
I'll take note of that.

93
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:41,600
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

94
00:05:44,633 --> 00:05:46,700
[MUSIC FADES]

95
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:53,700
- "Victor "Tiger" Zafra"
- [PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:06:03,567 --> 00:06:05,067
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

97
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:11,233
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

98
00:06:14,467 --> 00:06:16,167
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

99
00:06:18,967 --> 00:06:20,100
- [GABO SCREAMS]
- [TEKLA AND FRIENDS SHRIEK]

100
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:21,633
- Ow! Ow! Ow!
- What the hell, Gabo?!

101
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,767
It's just us! Your friends!

102
00:06:23,867 --> 00:06:25,300
[COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

103
00:06:25,433 --> 00:06:28,333
- My heart...
- You almost stabbed me!

104
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:29,567
What are you doing here?

105
00:06:29,667 --> 00:06:31,567
Where the hell were you?!

106
00:06:31,667 --> 00:06:34,000
You just disappeared!
We were so worried!

107
00:06:34,667 --> 00:06:35,900
[TOLITS] Uh, Gabo?

108
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,767
A-Are you still mad at us?
I'm so sorry for what I said.

109
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:45,700
I'm not mad anymore.
Forget about it.

110
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:48,667
Okay, come in.

111
00:06:48,833 --> 00:06:50,167
[BINOY] Put that machete away!

112
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,800
[TEKLA]
Gosh, why do you have that?

113
00:06:52,900 --> 00:06:56,367
- You scared us.
- You almost hit me, Gabo!

114
00:06:56,533 --> 00:06:57,800
[BINOY CLEARS THROAT]

115
00:06:59,367 --> 00:07:01,800
What's that? A school project?

116
00:07:03,067 --> 00:07:04,300
[MUSIC FADES]

117
00:07:06,967 --> 00:07:10,667
When we went back to the bar
to get our clothes,

118
00:07:10,833 --> 00:07:12,700
the owner was so furious

119
00:07:12,867 --> 00:07:15,000
because of what you did
to their customers.

120
00:07:15,167 --> 00:07:17,700
If we show up there again,
they said they'd press charges.

121
00:07:17,833 --> 00:07:19,967
Where were you anyway, Gabo?

122
00:07:24,733 --> 00:07:26,867
Something happened.

123
00:07:30,067 --> 00:07:31,367
- I was abducted.
- Huh?

124
00:07:31,533 --> 00:07:32,533
- Huh?!
- What?!

125
00:07:33,433 --> 00:07:34,567
Wh-Who?!

126
00:07:34,733 --> 00:07:36,033
I don't know them.

127
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:39,200
But I remember seeing them
in prison.

128
00:07:39,333 --> 00:07:41,900
Why did they abduct you?

129
00:07:42,067 --> 00:07:43,800
And how did you get away?

130
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:47,333
It's a long story.

131
00:07:49,067 --> 00:07:50,900
I'll tell you everything later.

132
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:55,833
Earlier, while I was alone here,

133
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:58,200
someone knocked on the door.

134
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:01,233
They left this parcel outside.

135
00:08:01,367 --> 00:08:02,433
What's inside?

136
00:08:02,567 --> 00:08:05,433
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

137
00:08:05,567 --> 00:08:06,867
A mission.

138
00:08:08,133 --> 00:08:09,933
It's a job for me.

139
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:12,900
Mission? What kind of mission?

140
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:20,067
Hunting down people
who have broken the law.

141
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,500
They want you to
hunt people down?

142
00:08:22,667 --> 00:08:26,433
I've seen that in foreign films!
What's it called? Mission...

143
00:08:26,567 --> 00:08:28,567
What's it called? Mission...

144
00:08:28,667 --> 00:08:30,133
Just like James Bond!

145
00:08:30,267 --> 00:08:31,967
- He's like James Bond!
- James Bond?

146
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:34,700
<i> Mission Is Possible?!</i>

147
00:08:34,833 --> 00:08:36,800
You're wrong!

148
00:08:36,967 --> 00:08:39,733
He's more like Agent 00!

149
00:08:39,833 --> 00:08:42,633
Don't make things up.
I've never heard of Agent 00.

150
00:08:42,767 --> 00:08:44,967
Don't you know Weng Weng?
The short guy?

151
00:08:45,133 --> 00:08:46,733
He's the Philippines'
James Bond.

152
00:08:46,833 --> 00:08:50,300
He uses an umbrella
to jump over buildings.

153
00:08:50,433 --> 00:08:52,267
Your James Bond
doesn't hold a candle to him.

154
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:56,467
Oh, I remember now.
That's a really old show.

155
00:08:56,633 --> 00:08:57,967
- Back in your days, right?
- Yeah.

156
00:08:58,100 --> 00:09:00,800
Wow, Gabo!
You've really come so far!

157
00:09:00,933 --> 00:09:05,233
You're now a secret agent
hunting down outlaws!

158
00:09:05,367 --> 00:09:06,733
What a glow-up!

159
00:09:06,867 --> 00:09:10,133
Yeah, that's basically
what my job is going to be.

160
00:09:10,267 --> 00:09:11,667
That's so cool!

161
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:15,167
Gabo, can you recommend us
to your bosses?

162
00:09:15,300 --> 00:09:17,767
- We can go on missions, too.
- Mm-hmm.

163
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,333
Uh... [CLEARS THROAT]

164
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:23,100
How much are we talking?

165
00:09:26,033 --> 00:09:27,333
One hundred thousand pesos.

166
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:29,167
- One hundred thousand?!
- One hundred thousand?

167
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:32,300
- Wow, that's a huge amount.
- A hundred thousand?

168
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:36,700
Gabo, how will we split the pay
if we find those men?

169
00:09:36,833 --> 00:09:40,300
Fifty percent will go to me.

170
00:09:41,667 --> 00:09:45,267
You can share
the other 50 percent.

171
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:50,700
- That's if you'll help me.
- Oh! I'm definitely in, Gabo.

172
00:09:50,867 --> 00:09:53,200
I'd rather be a secret agent
than be unemployed.

173
00:09:53,333 --> 00:09:54,800
Hey, we're in too.

174
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,600
Gabo, count us in.

175
00:09:56,733 --> 00:09:58,000
[TOLITS] Count us in, too!

176
00:09:58,133 --> 00:10:01,533
We're in!
I'm sure you can use our help.

177
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:03,400
[BINOY] So, we're settled?

178
00:10:03,533 --> 00:10:04,833
Okay.

179
00:10:05,833 --> 00:10:07,167
If you're up for the job,

180
00:10:08,833 --> 00:10:11,333
let's search for this man
tomorrow.

181
00:10:11,433 --> 00:10:14,367
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

182
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:20,067
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

183
00:10:20,067 --> 00:10:23,967
[FOOTSTEPS SHUFFLING]

184
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,100
[CLEARS THROAT]

185
00:10:26,100 --> 00:10:27,367
Sam!

186
00:10:27,367 --> 00:10:29,833
[CLEARS THROAT] Sam, Sam!

187
00:10:30,233 --> 00:10:31,833
[CLEARS THROAT] Sam...

188
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:34,500
[CREAKS]

189
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:35,733
Congrats, Sam.

190
00:10:37,133 --> 00:10:38,533
Congrats for what?

191
00:10:39,233 --> 00:10:40,867
For the briefing earlier?

192
00:10:40,867 --> 00:10:42,533
Don't we do those normally?

193
00:10:42,533 --> 00:10:43,767
Oh, no, no.

194
00:10:43,767 --> 00:10:45,733
Congrats because, um...

195
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:49,433
I know that our mission
is going to be successful.

196
00:10:49,933 --> 00:10:51,300
I can already see it!

197
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:53,233
[CHUCKLES] Wow.

198
00:10:53,233 --> 00:10:55,133
So you have a super power, huh?

199
00:10:55,133 --> 00:10:57,433
Oh, you!

200
00:10:57,433 --> 00:11:00,400
[SQUEALING] Didn't know
you have a funny bone!

201
00:11:01,867 --> 00:11:03,567
I'm glad I could bring out
this side of you.

202
00:11:03,567 --> 00:11:06,867
Oh, but on our mission,
I'll stick to you always.

203
00:11:08,333 --> 00:11:11,100
I'll be your knight
in shining armor.

204
00:11:11,933 --> 00:11:14,300
Because you don't know
what'll happen on our mission.

205
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:16,133
Maybe someone
will mess with you.

206
00:11:16,333 --> 00:11:18,233
Or you could be kissed
randomly again!

207
00:11:18,233 --> 00:11:20,933
I'll hit those bastards
with my uppercut!

208
00:11:20,933 --> 00:11:22,267
- Right? You know I can!
- [CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

209
00:11:22,267 --> 00:11:24,100
You need my protection, Sam.

210
00:11:24,467 --> 00:11:28,067
You know what, I don't need
your protection.

211
00:11:28,067 --> 00:11:31,233
Should those things
happen to me again,

212
00:11:32,067 --> 00:11:34,267
I'll slap them back to back.

213
00:11:35,167 --> 00:11:37,400
I hope your super powers
saw that one coming.

214
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:39,100
[SQUEALING MOCKINGLY]

215
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:46,067
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

216
00:11:46,867 --> 00:11:48,267
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

217
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:53,067
[MAX] Dad, so many people
got injured in Ginintuang Lupa.

218
00:11:53,367 --> 00:11:56,033
Good thing the mayor's men
arrived on time

219
00:11:56,033 --> 00:11:57,900
to put a stop to the demolition.

220
00:11:58,967 --> 00:12:00,433
This won't end today.

221
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:03,267
There will be more men

222
00:12:03,633 --> 00:12:06,267
for the next demolition
in Ginintuang Lupa.

223
00:12:06,267 --> 00:12:07,567
[ISOBEL] Um...

224
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:10,267
Whatever the kind of solution
you'll come up with,

225
00:12:10,467 --> 00:12:15,233
just make sure that our family
won't be involved physically.

226
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:20,000
- [ISOBEL BREATHES DEEPLY]
- [FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

227
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,967
- Sam! Let's eat.
- [ISOBEL] Oh!

228
00:12:22,333 --> 00:12:23,467
[ISOBEL] Sweetie,

229
00:12:23,733 --> 00:12:25,000
have you eaten yet?

230
00:12:26,367 --> 00:12:27,533
[SAM] I have.

231
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:30,467
Dad.

232
00:12:33,533 --> 00:12:35,633
Uh... I'll just go upstairs.

233
00:12:37,167 --> 00:12:38,967
Anyway, Dad, if you ever
need anything,

234
00:12:38,967 --> 00:12:40,533
the police is ready
to help, okay?

235
00:12:40,533 --> 00:12:42,000
[RICARDO] And I'm telling you,

236
00:12:42,567 --> 00:12:45,533
if they want this demolition
to be even bloodier,

237
00:12:46,333 --> 00:12:47,933
I'll give it to them!

238
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:51,400
[RICARDO] I'll be happy
to accommodate.

239
00:12:52,333 --> 00:12:53,400
[SAM, VOICE BREAKING] Uh...

240
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:55,067
Excuse me, wait a second.

241
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:57,133
The demolition was bloody?

242
00:12:57,533 --> 00:13:00,300
I thought we put the operation
aside for now?

243
00:13:00,533 --> 00:13:03,333
It already happened, Sam.
It just didn't push through.

244
00:13:03,333 --> 00:13:06,233
Exactly. I thought we're not
going to drive them out anymore.

245
00:13:06,233 --> 00:13:08,233
Why do you care about
those people so much?

246
00:13:08,233 --> 00:13:09,400
[ISOBEL WHISPERING] Ricardo...

247
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:13,400
The people in Ginintuang Lupa
are nothing but trash!

248
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:15,100
All I know is that it's going
to cause us problems

249
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:17,033
if we rush them
into leaving the area.

250
00:13:17,033 --> 00:13:19,233
- [CLATTERS]
- Oh my god. Enough, Ricardo.

251
00:13:19,233 --> 00:13:21,400
Those good for nothings
are thugs

252
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:24,167
and are completely useless
to our society.

253
00:13:24,633 --> 00:13:28,633
I'm even doing God's work
in driving those pests away!

254
00:13:28,633 --> 00:13:30,900
[SAM] They might be poor,

255
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:32,467
but they're still human.

256
00:13:32,467 --> 00:13:34,200
And I hope we treat them
like one!

257
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:36,333
They're living off
of my property.

258
00:13:37,367 --> 00:13:39,200
They don't deserve any mercy!

259
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:43,600
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

260
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:45,233
So if you don't know enough,

261
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,667
it's best you shut up.

262
00:13:48,933 --> 00:13:50,233
[ISOBEL SOBS]

263
00:13:55,633 --> 00:13:57,233
- Sam!
- [CHAIR RATTLES]

264
00:13:57,467 --> 00:13:58,567
Sit down.

265
00:13:59,233 --> 00:14:00,567
- [MAX] Excuse me.
- Sit down.

266
00:14:00,567 --> 00:14:01,967
- Samantha!
- [DOOR OPENS]

267
00:14:01,967 --> 00:14:03,933
- Sam!
- [DOOR SLAMS CLOSE]

268
00:14:03,933 --> 00:14:10,900
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

269
00:14:17,733 --> 00:14:19,300
[DOOR SQUEAKS OPEN]

270
00:14:19,933 --> 00:14:21,067
You okay?

271
00:14:25,233 --> 00:14:26,233
Sam.

272
00:14:26,633 --> 00:14:29,567
Dad has a point, okay?

273
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:32,467
He owns the land,
so he can do whatever he wants.

274
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:34,967
Sure, he can.

275
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:38,433
I just thought that
maybe he should pause

276
00:14:38,433 --> 00:14:40,167
and think about the people.

277
00:14:40,167 --> 00:14:42,133
Especially those who live there.

278
00:14:42,133 --> 00:14:44,267
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

279
00:14:44,267 --> 00:14:45,300
[SIGHS]

280
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:47,867
[PHONE RINGING]

281
00:14:47,867 --> 00:14:48,967
[MAX] Who's that?

282
00:14:49,333 --> 00:14:50,300
- Well?
- No one.

283
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:51,333
Who is it?

284
00:14:51,867 --> 00:14:53,867
- Come on, give it to me.
- No, no...

285
00:14:53,867 --> 00:14:56,000
- Why not answer it?
- No need.

286
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,633
- It's not work-related.
- Come on, answer.

287
00:14:57,633 --> 00:14:59,533
Ah, so it's personal.

288
00:14:59,533 --> 00:15:00,500
[RINGING CONTINUES]

289
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:02,100
He's been wooing you for ages.

290
00:15:02,133 --> 00:15:03,500
When will you say yes?

291
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:04,533
Why would I?

292
00:15:04,533 --> 00:15:06,533
I don't have any feelings
for him.

293
00:15:06,533 --> 00:15:08,667
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

294
00:15:08,667 --> 00:15:09,967
[MAX] Hmm?

295
00:15:09,967 --> 00:15:11,000
[CHUCKLES]

296
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Oh, come on.

297
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,567
You know what they say?

298
00:15:13,567 --> 00:15:15,200
- Hmm, what?
- In love,

299
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:17,700
you'll feel a hundred emotions.

300
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:20,000
Joy, excitement, nervousness...

301
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,567
All mixed together.

302
00:15:21,567 --> 00:15:23,067
But when it comes to Seb,

303
00:15:23,067 --> 00:15:25,000
there's only one thing
I feel toward him.

304
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,467
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

305
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:28,200
- Annoyance.
- Really?

306
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:29,633
- Mm-hmm.
- I know you.

307
00:15:29,633 --> 00:15:31,233
He's exactly your type.

308
00:15:31,233 --> 00:15:33,500
Clean, decent, formal.

309
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:35,467
Me, I like bad boys.

310
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:37,267
Don't drag it out.

311
00:15:37,267 --> 00:15:39,467
He'll end up being your
boyfriend, I'm telling you.

312
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:41,500
You know, I'm not in a hurry.

313
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:44,067
Why are you pressuring me?

314
00:15:44,067 --> 00:15:45,533
I'm a very beautiful woman.

315
00:15:45,533 --> 00:15:47,400
There are other guys
waiting for me.

316
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:48,667
A whole lot of them.

317
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:51,700
- Hmm?
- No, just kidding.

318
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:52,667
[GIGGLES]

319
00:15:52,667 --> 00:15:54,167
That was a joke?

320
00:15:54,700 --> 00:15:58,233
Ah, you're into some guy,
but you're not telling me.

321
00:15:58,233 --> 00:16:00,067
- Not true! Come on...
- Who is it?

322
00:16:00,067 --> 00:16:01,500
- No one!
- Just tell me.

323
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:04,067
Nobody! Okay, go away now!

324
00:16:04,067 --> 00:16:05,733
I still need to review my cases.

325
00:16:05,733 --> 00:16:06,700
[MAX] Hmm?

326
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:08,367
What? [GIGGLES]
Just go!

327
00:16:09,367 --> 00:16:11,533
If I find out something,
you'll see.

328
00:16:11,533 --> 00:16:13,467
- Go with your bad boys.
- Whatever.

329
00:16:13,467 --> 00:16:15,467
- Alright, good night.
- Bye.

330
00:16:15,467 --> 00:16:16,600
Hmm?

331
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,600
[BOTH GIGGLING]

332
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,600
- You sure?
- Just drop it! Bye-bye!

333
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:22,267
[MAX] Poor guy.
Give him your answer!

334
00:16:22,267 --> 00:16:23,367
Good night.

335
00:16:23,367 --> 00:16:24,367
[DOOR CLOSES]

336
00:16:24,367 --> 00:16:31,333
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

337
00:16:36,267 --> 00:16:38,733
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [CAR HORN HONKING]

338
00:16:38,733 --> 00:16:40,533
[DOOR SQUEAKS CLOSE]

339
00:16:40,533 --> 00:16:42,667
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

340
00:16:44,633 --> 00:16:46,267
[SALVADOR] Hey, Oli.

341
00:16:46,267 --> 00:16:47,433
What's the problem?

342
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:49,633
Where is it?

343
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:50,667
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

344
00:16:50,667 --> 00:16:51,667
Hey.

345
00:16:51,667 --> 00:16:52,800
Wait, wait, wait.

346
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:54,500
I said what's the problem?

347
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:56,300
- [BANGS TABLE]
- [INHALES DEEPLY]

348
00:16:56,300 --> 00:16:57,467
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

349
00:16:58,233 --> 00:16:59,433
[GRUNTING]

350
00:16:59,433 --> 00:17:00,600
[INHALES DEEPLY]

351
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,000
[OLI] Salvador.

352
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,267
The person we interviewed
last night...

353
00:17:06,633 --> 00:17:08,167
The one whose spouse was shot?

354
00:17:08,167 --> 00:17:09,400
Well, what happened?

355
00:17:10,067 --> 00:17:12,300
Let's present it to Boss Arnel.

356
00:17:12,300 --> 00:17:14,667
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

357
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:16,667
- [BREATHES DEEPLY]
- [KEYBOARD CLACKING]

358
00:17:17,533 --> 00:17:21,133
Don't tell me you didn't get
the interview on record, Oli.

359
00:17:24,167 --> 00:17:26,667
[ARNEL] What?! You failed
to record it, Oli?!

360
00:17:26,667 --> 00:17:27,667
[SIGHS EXASPERATEDLY]

361
00:17:29,167 --> 00:17:30,100
Boss...

362
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:33,300
You know the consequence
of that mistake!

363
00:17:34,167 --> 00:17:37,167
Boss... Boss, have mercy!

364
00:17:37,167 --> 00:17:39,333
Boss, my wife just gave birth!

365
00:17:39,333 --> 00:17:41,700
I'm the only one providing
for them. Besides, boss--

366
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:43,433
Boss, I have a side chick!

367
00:17:43,433 --> 00:17:46,267
I cover her internet bill, boss!

368
00:17:46,267 --> 00:17:48,700
I'm the one supporting
them all, boss!

369
00:17:48,733 --> 00:17:50,700
- Boss, I can't lose this job!
- Let me go--

370
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:52,500
- Stay away!
- I'm begging you!

371
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:54,367
I don't want any excuses!

372
00:17:55,167 --> 00:17:57,667
If you make a mistake,
you're fired!

373
00:17:58,467 --> 00:18:00,167
[SALVADOR] Boss, boss, boss.

374
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:01,867
Calm down, boss. Calm down.

375
00:18:01,867 --> 00:18:04,700
Let's give him a second chance.
He's nice.

376
00:18:05,300 --> 00:18:06,367
[ARNEL SIGHING]

377
00:18:06,367 --> 00:18:09,133
He's in my hands, boss.
He's my responsibility.

378
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:11,867
Don't worry.
I'll fix this, boss.

379
00:18:11,867 --> 00:18:14,233
I need news that
will attract viewers.

380
00:18:14,233 --> 00:18:15,633
[SALVADOR]
We'll do another interview

381
00:18:15,633 --> 00:18:17,267
with the victim's family.

382
00:18:18,133 --> 00:18:20,567
I promise you, boss.
This will be a hit.

383
00:18:20,567 --> 00:18:22,667
Everyone will see it,

384
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:25,233
and it'll be the interview
of a lifetime.

385
00:18:25,233 --> 00:18:26,767
That's my promise, boss.

386
00:18:26,767 --> 00:18:28,433
Just don't fire him.

387
00:18:28,433 --> 00:18:30,267
Be grateful, Oli,

388
00:18:30,267 --> 00:18:32,067
that Salvador came
to your rescue.

389
00:18:33,200 --> 00:18:34,733
I'll give you another chance!

390
00:18:34,733 --> 00:18:36,500
But I'm coming along this time.

391
00:18:37,533 --> 00:18:40,100
I don't want sloppy work

392
00:18:40,100 --> 00:18:42,767
on the jobs that feed
your families,

393
00:18:42,767 --> 00:18:44,200
and your mistress!

394
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:46,400
Boss, someone might hear you.

395
00:18:46,733 --> 00:18:48,700
That woman is hideous.

396
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:49,667
That's harsh.

397
00:18:49,667 --> 00:18:51,833
I love her, and that's all
that matters.

398
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:55,267
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

399
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:56,567
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

400
00:18:56,567 --> 00:18:57,600
[TWINKLE] Ma'am?

401
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:58,533
[DOOR OPENS]

402
00:18:59,867 --> 00:19:01,433
- Ma'am?
- [SAM] Twinkle.

403
00:19:01,433 --> 00:19:03,233
- Good morning.
- Please, let me help you.

404
00:19:03,233 --> 00:19:04,900
- Oh no, thank you.
- Huh?

405
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:06,267
It's okay. I got it.

406
00:19:06,267 --> 00:19:07,267
Why?

407
00:19:07,267 --> 00:19:09,533
Well, you didn't eat last night.

408
00:19:09,533 --> 00:19:11,533
You also didn't tell me

409
00:19:11,533 --> 00:19:13,600
what time you were going
to wake up,

410
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:15,600
or if you'd have breakfast.

411
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:16,667
So...

412
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:19,567
I took the initiative
to check on you.

413
00:19:20,533 --> 00:19:22,767
Why did you get up early today?

414
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:25,200
I need to be at the office.

415
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:27,233
I have a lot of important things
to finish.

416
00:19:27,433 --> 00:19:28,567
Oh.

417
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:32,167
Ooh! Looks like you're going
to have a busy day!

418
00:19:32,167 --> 00:19:35,300
That's why
you'd better head downstairs,

419
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:39,233
eat breakfast to keep you
energized throughout the day!

420
00:19:39,633 --> 00:19:41,533
Right? And great timing, ma'am.

421
00:19:41,767 --> 00:19:43,600
Your mother
is already downstairs.

422
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:44,800
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

423
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:46,567
[EXHALES] I'll skip breakfast.

424
00:19:46,567 --> 00:19:48,367
- I'll just say goodbye to them.
- Huh?

425
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:50,267
[DOOR OPENS]

426
00:19:53,433 --> 00:19:56,367
Hey, everything should be ready.

427
00:19:56,633 --> 00:19:58,433
Once Ricardo gets down,

428
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:00,267
serve him
hot coffee immediately.

429
00:20:00,267 --> 00:20:02,600
Oh, what else is in the kitchen?

430
00:20:02,867 --> 00:20:04,233
Good morning, Mom.

431
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:05,933
- I'll get going.
- Huh?

432
00:20:06,333 --> 00:20:08,300
What? You're leaving?

433
00:20:08,833 --> 00:20:11,733
It's bad getting used
to skipping breakfast.

434
00:20:12,333 --> 00:20:14,267
I've got things to take care of
in the office.

435
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:15,733
Oh, really?

436
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,400
Then tell me about it.

437
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:18,633
Have a seat.

438
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:20,833
- [CHUCKLES HESITANTLY]
- Come on.

439
00:20:25,500 --> 00:20:26,467
[CHAIR DRAGS]

440
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:29,433
Now, tell me.

441
00:20:29,633 --> 00:20:32,600
So, why is my youngest
always in a hurry?

442
00:20:33,367 --> 00:20:36,167
We're handling a huge case
in NCIA.

443
00:20:36,667 --> 00:20:37,967
It's a gold smuggling case.

444
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:41,900
This is our only chance
to catch those syndicates.

445
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:44,800
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- A gold smuggling case.

446
00:20:45,533 --> 00:20:48,267
Goodness, that's no joke.

447
00:20:48,733 --> 00:20:50,667
Are you sure youre safe
with that?

448
00:20:51,833 --> 00:20:53,300
- [RICARDO CLEARS THROAT]
- Oh!

449
00:20:53,300 --> 00:20:55,333
Oh, Ricardo, your daughter here

450
00:20:55,633 --> 00:20:58,300
is after a syndicate.

451
00:21:03,733 --> 00:21:05,467
Sam got that after you.

452
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:09,733
Worrying about small matters

453
00:21:09,767 --> 00:21:11,667
we shouldn't even
be thinking about.

454
00:21:13,833 --> 00:21:16,900
The case I'm leading has been
researched by the team well.

455
00:21:17,733 --> 00:21:19,633
That's why I'll be safe, Mom.

456
00:21:22,733 --> 00:21:25,033
Ricardo, don't you have
anything else to say, like...

457
00:21:25,667 --> 00:21:27,000
at least some advice.

458
00:21:27,567 --> 00:21:28,433
Anything.

459
00:21:28,433 --> 00:21:30,700
It's just another day
in the office.

460
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:32,733
When I was her age,

461
00:21:33,567 --> 00:21:35,867
I had dealt
with a much more serious case.

462
00:21:38,333 --> 00:21:39,633
Well, Sam...

463
00:21:40,267 --> 00:21:42,700
the fact that you are the lead
in this operation--

464
00:21:43,467 --> 00:21:44,833
I just want you to know that

465
00:21:45,033 --> 00:21:46,933
me and your Dad
are so proud of you.

466
00:21:47,467 --> 00:21:48,533
[CUTLERY CLANKS]

467
00:21:48,767 --> 00:21:49,933
[RICARDO] Isobel.

468
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:54,367
Easy on boosting
your daughter's confidence.

469
00:21:54,567 --> 00:21:57,400
That can get to her head.
She hasn't proven anything yet.

470
00:21:57,767 --> 00:22:02,300
[MUSIC TURNS MELLOW]

471
00:22:02,300 --> 00:22:03,667
[CUTLERY CLANKS]

472
00:22:18,633 --> 00:22:20,900
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

473
00:22:24,433 --> 00:22:26,300
[SAM] Team,
we have been planning

474
00:22:26,433 --> 00:22:27,267
for this day for a long time.

475
00:22:27,433 --> 00:22:29,200
Let's do our best
to catch the target.

476
00:22:29,600 --> 00:22:30,900
- Yes, ma'am!
- Yes, maam!

477
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:33,433
Let's keep our communication
lines open.

478
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:35,600
Once you see the target,
notify us immediately.

479
00:22:36,733 --> 00:22:42,067
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

480
00:22:42,233 --> 00:22:43,367
[TONY] Ma'am.

481
00:22:43,467 --> 00:22:46,900
the warrants for Mr. Chan
and Victor Zafra are here.

482
00:22:47,267 --> 00:22:53,400
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

483
00:22:53,533 --> 00:22:54,600
Let's go.

484
00:22:55,267 --> 00:22:56,267
[CLEARS THROAT]

485
00:22:56,533 --> 00:22:58,167
Team Leader Sam.

486
00:23:00,767 --> 00:23:02,000
Get ready, okay?

487
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:04,433
Don't mess this up.

488
00:23:04,933 --> 00:23:06,000
We're ready, ma'am.

489
00:23:06,933 --> 00:23:08,167
Thank you for the confidence.

490
00:23:08,300 --> 00:23:10,133
You can thank me later

491
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:13,967
once you've brought
the targets here.

492
00:23:14,133 --> 00:23:15,467
That is,

493
00:23:16,633 --> 00:23:17,767
if you can actually
bring them.

494
00:23:22,533 --> 00:23:23,467
Pia.

495
00:23:24,733 --> 00:23:25,833
My office. Now.

496
00:23:25,967 --> 00:23:31,300
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

497
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:32,700
[SIGHS]

498
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:38,100
Sam.

499
00:23:39,633 --> 00:23:41,667
Team Alpha,
good luck to you.

500
00:23:41,800 --> 00:23:45,133
I know you won't let
the agency down.

501
00:23:46,533 --> 00:23:47,767
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

502
00:23:48,800 --> 00:23:49,833
Let's move!

503
00:23:49,967 --> 00:23:56,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

504
00:24:02,733 --> 00:24:03,700
[OMENG] Pops.

505
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:05,500
Gabo took the mission.

506
00:24:06,033 --> 00:24:06,967
[TOMAS] The real question is...

507
00:24:07,067 --> 00:24:08,533
will he do it?

508
00:24:08,700 --> 00:24:11,367
I'm sure that Gabo
will chicken out.

509
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:14,967
Let's find someone else, pops.

510
00:24:15,067 --> 00:24:16,533
Give him some time.

511
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:19,333
I have strong faith

512
00:24:19,433 --> 00:24:21,533
that Gabo will carry out
the mission.

513
00:24:22,167 --> 00:24:29,133
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

514
00:24:29,867 --> 00:24:31,200
[KNIFE SWISHES]

515
00:24:33,100 --> 00:24:35,400
[KNIFE SWISHES]

516
00:24:40,367 --> 00:24:41,833
[RUBBER STRETCHING]

517
00:24:43,267 --> 00:24:47,200
[METAL RATTLING]

518
00:24:50,600 --> 00:24:51,667
[SWISHES]

519
00:24:54,033 --> 00:24:55,600
[METAL RATTLING, SWISHES]

520
00:24:55,767 --> 00:24:56,733
[THUDS]

521
00:24:56,867 --> 00:25:03,700
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

522
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:18,033
The patient
is in critical condition.

523
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:19,967
<i>He needs to be
operated on immediately.</i>

524
00:25:20,467 --> 00:25:22,600
<i> This job will be a huge help.</i>

525
00:25:22,767 --> 00:25:24,067
<i> It won't just be for you...</i>

526
00:25:24,767 --> 00:25:27,700
<i>it will also change
your family's life.</i>

527
00:25:27,967 --> 00:25:29,633
<i> Your spouse is dying!</i>

528
00:25:29,767 --> 00:25:31,767
<i>Give it your all.
Three, two, one, action!</i>

529
00:25:31,933 --> 00:25:33,100
[WAILING]

530
00:25:33,267 --> 00:25:35,767
<i> We need your help,</i>

531
00:25:35,967 --> 00:25:37,400
<i> we don't have any money!</i>

532
00:25:37,500 --> 00:25:39,500
- [WAILING]
- We need your he--

533
00:25:39,633 --> 00:25:40,133
<i> Hey!</i>

534
00:25:40,300 --> 00:25:41,933
[NARRATOR] Two groups.

535
00:25:42,033 --> 00:25:43,233
<i>- Hey!
- Hey!</i>

536
00:25:43,333 --> 00:25:45,600
<i>- That hurt!
- Are you blind?!</i>

537
00:25:45,700 --> 00:25:48,133
<i>Am I blind? I'm huge.
How could you not see me?</i>

538
00:25:48,300 --> 00:25:49,433
<i> Whoa, he's fiesty!</i>

539
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:50,567
<i> Are you underestimating us?</i>

540
00:25:50,667 --> 00:25:52,433
<i> Two, three, four...</i>

541
00:25:52,600 --> 00:25:55,267
[SINGING] Filipinos come on
and join in!

542
00:25:55,433 --> 00:25:57,600
<i> Kung Hei Fat Choy!</i>

543
00:25:57,767 --> 00:26:00,433
[SINGING] Filipinos come on
and join in!

544
00:26:00,533 --> 00:26:02,933
<i> Kung Hei Fat Choy!</i>

545
00:26:03,100 --> 00:26:04,300
[NARRATOR] One mission.

546
00:26:04,467 --> 00:26:05,133
<i> Team.</i>

547
00:26:05,300 --> 00:26:06,400
<i> The target is coming out.</i>

548
00:26:06,967 --> 00:26:08,433
<i> Visuals on target.</i>

549
00:26:10,167 --> 00:26:11,467
<i> We'll follow him.</i>

550
00:26:14,500 --> 00:26:16,533
<i>Mr. Chan will lead us
to Tiger.</i>

551
00:26:16,667 --> 00:26:19,133
<i>We'll follow him
and trap them there.</i>

552
00:26:20,333 --> 00:26:22,367
<i> We need to catch Tiger.</i>

553
00:26:22,833 --> 00:26:24,933
<i>Are you sure about the
work we are doing?</i>

554
00:26:25,033 --> 00:26:26,667
<i> I hope we get paid well.</i>

555
00:26:26,833 --> 00:26:28,333
<i>Our lives might be
at risk here, Gabo.</i>

556
00:26:28,500 --> 00:26:29,433
<i> Sam. Positive.</i>

557
00:26:29,533 --> 00:26:30,767
[NARRATOR]<i> Will they
</i> work together...

558
00:26:30,867 --> 00:26:34,133
<i>They have millions of pesos
and gold in there!</i>

559
00:26:34,233 --> 00:26:35,467
[NARRATOR] or will they clash?

560
00:26:35,633 --> 00:26:37,533
<i>- Excuse me!
- Ouch! Ouch!</i>

561
00:26:37,667 --> 00:26:39,133
<i>- You again?!
- What do you mean?!</i>

562
00:26:39,233 --> 00:26:40,433
<i> You're so rude!</i>

563
00:26:41,333 --> 00:26:42,333
<i>Hey, do you want me
to kiss you?</i>

564
00:26:42,533 --> 00:26:43,500
<i>- Jerk!
- [GROANS] Argh!</i>

565
00:26:43,667 --> 00:26:44,833
<i> Hey, you jerk!</i>

566
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:46,900
<i>Do you know that
I'm an NCIA agent?!</i>

567
00:26:49,733 --> 00:26:50,633
[ENGINE REVVS]

568
00:26:50,733 --> 00:26:51,867
<i> Catch them!</i>

569
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:52,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

570
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:53,800
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

571
00:26:53,900 --> 00:26:55,800
- [TIRES SCREECH]
- [ENGINE REVVS]

572
00:26:56,400 --> 00:26:58,033
- [TRUCK HORN BLARING]
- [CRASHES]

573
00:26:58,167 --> 00:27:00,233
[NARRATOR] The King of Tondo.

574
00:27:00,400 --> 00:27:02,800
[NARRATOR]<i> We're going all out
</i> in this clash.

575
00:27:03,100 --> 00:27:04,300
[GROANS] Argh!

576
00:27:05,367 --> 00:27:06,500
[METAL ROD CLANGS]

577
00:27:06,600 --> 00:27:08,667
[GROANS] Argh!

578
00:27:11,333 --> 00:27:12,733
[GLASS BREAKING]
